# Segmented Development Log

After completing any coding task (feature, bug fix, refactor, UI update, documentation, configuration, database, testing, or architecture change), update the development log before ending your response.

Use the **segmented-development-log** skill (`@segmented-development-log`).

## Requirements

- Log path: `docs/development_logs/`
- One Markdown file per 3-day calendar period: `YYYY-MM-DD_to_YYYY-MM-DD.md`
- **Append only** — never overwrite, delete, reorder, or summarize previous entries
- Document only files actually created, modified, renamed, or deleted
- Ignore viewed-only files, reverted changes, and unimplemented plans
- Read the active period log first, then append chronologically at the end
- Update **Last Updated** in the file header when appending
- Use templates from `~/.cursor/skills/segmented-development-log/entry-template.md`

Skip logging only when: no file changes occurred, the task was question/plan/review-only, or the user says not to log.
